WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.780
Anandpur, 1699.

2
00:00:02.830 --> 00:00:06.270
A crowd gathers for the
spring festival of Vaisakhi.

3
00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:09.560
Guru Gobind Singh asks
who will offer their life.

4
00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:12.740
One by one, five Sikhs step forward.

5
00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:16.340
Today, five Sikhs still
lead a ceremony with water,

6
00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:19.560
sugar, a sword and one iron bowl.

7
00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:22.800
So why do some Sikhs drink
from one shared bowl,

8
00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:25.050
and promise never to cut their hair?

9
00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:27.850
In this mission, you'll meet the Five Ks:

10
00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:30.600
a uniform of identity and commitment.

11
00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:35.530
Then you'll compare how initiated and
non-initiated Sikhs see these symbols,

12
00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:38.230
and weigh up what makes a true Sikh.

13
00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:43.070
Your mission: find out why some Sikhs
share one bowl and promise never to cut

14
00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:43.810
their hair.
